# Frame sequences are now REAL assets, not §9 placeholders, so they are
# tracked — the site cannot render without them and there is no build step
# that would produce them at deploy time.
#
# They come from scripts/render-frames.py, which is deterministic, and are
# proven by scripts/verify-frames.py. 904 WebP, ~4.7MB.
#
# What stays ignored: iCloud conflict forks. This repo sits on a synced
# Desktop, and re-rendering races the sync daemon, which restores the files it
# just saw deleted under a duplicate name — `frame_0090 2.webp` beside
# `frame_0090.webp`. 706 of them (3.9MB of stale placeholder) were committed
# to nothing once already. render-frames.py prunes them and verify-frames.py
# fails on them; this is the third guard.
/public/seq/**/* [0-9].webp
/public/seq/**/*\ [0-9].webp
